Title: golden fixture attachments need a schema-compliant state/drift marker, not extra
Created: 2026-09-04
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-04T06:39Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Filed while running ticket 0632's real golden-fixture injection for the
first time. Zotero's own live schema (`GET /api/schema`, verified
2026-09-04) restricts the `attachment` item type to exactly `title`,
`accessDate`, `url` as data fields — `extra` is rejected outright: `400
"'extra' is not a valid field for type 'attachment'"`. `golden_fixture.py`'s
`_desired_attachment()` had, since it was first written, unconditionally
written a rich attestation string into `extra` on every attachment
(source sha256, role, relation, language, selection expectation, skip
reason, and a pending/reindexed extraction-state marker). This was never
validated against real Zotero before 2026-09-04 — the mocked test double
(`MemoryZotero`) enforces no field-legality rules at all — so the defect
sat invisible through every prior review and test run.

0632 fixed the immediate blocker (removed `extra` from the attachment
payload; commit on `t0632-golden-fixture-harness-verify`), which was
required to run at all. That fix is deliberately narrow: it drops the
capability the field used to carry rather than replacing it, because doing
so safely mid-real-run risked a second rushed, unverified change on top of
the first. This ticket is the properly-scoped follow-up.

## What was lost, precisely

1. **Crash-recovery marker.** The old design wrote a "pending" version of
   an attachment's `extra` before calling `reindex_fulltext`, then a
   "reindexed" version after. If the script crashed between those two
   writes, a re-run would see the mismatch and retry. Without it, a re-run
   after such a crash sees the attachment as already matching its desired
   state and will not retry — narrow window (only mid-poll), but real, and
   affects every future re-run of this harness, not just today's.
2. **Sha256-drift detection.** Nothing in `_desired_attachment()`'s output
   now depends on the recipe's pinned `sha256`. A correct re-pin — the
   source file AND `recipe.json`'s hash updated together, so
   `verify_source_bytes` sees no mismatch — silently does not force a
   re-upload or re-extraction, because `inject()`'s reconciliation
   (`_managed_equal`) has nothing left to detect the change with.
   `bench/fixtures/README.md`'s own documented "Re-pinning" procedure
   depends on this working. Pinned down as a red test:
   `tests/test_golden_fixture_harness.py::
   test_a_repin_with_no_local_hash_mismatch_is_not_yet_redetected`.

Both gaps are real (not hypothetical) and both matter more than "today's
one-off run" — the golden fixture is meant to be re-pinned and re-injected
repeatedly over the corpus's life (browser-only sources landing later,
occasional archive corrections). Neither blocks the very first, fresh
injection into an empty collection, which is why 0632 could ship without
them and still complete its own real run.

## Relevant files
- `bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py` — `_desired_attachment`, `inject`,
  `_refresh_fulltext_from_pinned_sources`, `_managed_markers`,
  `_require_only_managed_marker`, `ZoteroLocalClient.upload_file`
- `bench/fixtures/make_index_fixture.mjs` — `loadGoldenExport`'s mirrored
  validation (`requireFields`, `requireOnlyManagedMarker`)
- `tests/test_golden_fixture_harness.py` — the red test named above, plus
  `test_failed_reindex_leaves_attachment_pending_and_unexportable` (now
  documents rather than proves the crash-recovery gap)
- `bench/fixtures/README.md` — "Re-pinning" section, whose promise this
  ticket needs to keep actually true

## Actions (a starting sketch, not a spec)
1. Design a schema-compliant carrier for both signals. Tags are the
   only field Zotero's attachment schema leaves free-form and already
   proven (`SOURCE_TAG_PREFIX`, `ATTACHMENT_TAG_PREFIX`); a sha256 tag
   and/or a pending-state tag are the obvious candidates, but this needs a
   real design pass, not a copy of the identity-tag pattern verbatim —
   `_managed_markers`/`_require_only_managed_marker` currently assume
   "exactly one managed tag" per item, which a second tag category breaks
   for attachments specifically (parents stay single-marker). Consider
   also: does the local API's `imported_file` item data expose a real,
   Zotero-computed `md5` after upload registers, usable as a
   zero-new-tag drift signal for the group path specifically (verify
   against live Zotero, not assumed)? If so, `user`/`linked_file` still
   needs its own answer, since Zotero does not upload/hash linked files
   the same way.
2. Update both `golden_fixture.py` and `make_index_fixture.mjs` in lockstep
   (they already mirror each other's attachment-shape validation).
3. Turn the red test in `test_golden_fixture_harness.py` green; restore
   real coverage for the "reindex failed, subsequent export must refuse"
   scenario that `test_failed_reindex_leaves_attachment_pending_and_
   unexportable` had to relax.

## Test
- Start from the red test named above (already committed, already failing
  the *old* assertion until this ticket's fix lands — currently passing
  only because it asserts the gap, not the fix).

## Invariants
- `_managed_markers`/`_require_only_managed_marker` keep working correctly
  for PARENT items exactly as today (single identity marker); any
  generalization must not weaken parent-side reconciliation.
- The fix must be verified against Zotero's real schema/API behavior
  (`GET /api/schema`, a real local-API round trip), not only the mocked
  `MemoryZotero` test double — that is exactly the blind spot that let the
  original `extra` defect ship unnoticed.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] a schema-compliant mechanism restores crash-recovery detection
      (interrupted reindex is retried on the next run)
- [ ] a schema-compliant mechanism restores sha256-drift detection (a
      correct re-pin is detected and forces re-upload/re-extraction)
- [ ] `test_a_repin_with_no_local_hash_mismatch_is_not_yet_redetected` is
      rewritten to assert the restored (positive) behavior
- [ ] `test_failed_reindex_leaves_attachment_pending_and_unexportable`'s
      relaxed assertion is restored to a real one
- [ ] `bench/fixtures/README.md`'s "Re-pinning" section is re-verified true
      end to end (fetch → re-pin → re-inject → re-export), not just by
      inspection
